-- akn:att_7__hc_1/p3 The file number the page prints under the table (2015-33793); no rule.

`the seven tables of 1.1.2015` MEANS
    LIST `annex א'1 of 1.1.2015`, `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015`, `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015`, `annex א'4 of 1.1.2015`,
         `annex א'5 of 1.1.2015`, `annex א'6 of 1.1.2015`, `annex א'7 of 1.1.2015`

§§ `בדיקת הטבלאות`

-- (1) The day: every table prints the day the last allocation was put off
-- to.
#ASSERT `the tables of 1.1.2015 are updated from` EQUALS `the last allocation is put off to`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD t's `published table from` EQUALS `the tables of 1.1.2015 are updated from`) `the seven tables of 1.1.2015`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD `the published labels of` t EQUALS range 1 36) `the seven tables of 1.1.2015`

-- (2) The update. From 1.1.2015 the tables stand 6.35% above the tables in
-- force before 1.1.2011 (§92(ג) of the completion agreement, put off by the
-- agreement of 22.7.2013); the third part's tables stood 5.75% above the
-- same tables. Each cell beside the third part's cell at the same seniority
-- and grade raised by 1.0635/1.0575, to the agora (convention
-- rounding.half). The seven tables are the third part's א'1–א'7 in order.
`the rise of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables` MEANS
    (1 PLUS `the 2011 supplement rate from 1 July 2013`) DIVIDED BY (1 PLUS `the total update of the reform tables from 1.4.2013`)

GIVEN old IS A `salary table`
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the third part's cell raised to 1.1.2015 in` old IS
    GIVEN l, g YIELD
        CONSIDER `the pay at grade` g (`the row labelled` old l)
        WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`to the agora` (x TIMES `the rise of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables`))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

`the third part's tables, in the order of 1.1.2015` MEANS
    LIST `third-part annex א'1`, `third-part annex א'2`, `third-part annex א'3`, `third-part annex א'4`,
         `third-part annex א'5`, `third-part annex א'6`, `third-part annex א'7`

`the update checks of 1.1.2015` MEANS
    concat (zipWith (GIVEN new, old YIELD `the published cells beside` (`the third part's cell raised to 1.1.2015 in` old) `in` new)
                    `the seven tables of 1.1.2015` `the third part's tables, in the order of 1.1.2015`)

`the cells of 1.1.2015 the third part does not print` MEANS
    sum (zipWith (GIVEN new, old YIELD `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the third part's cell raised to 1.1.2015 in` old) `in` new)
                 `the seven tables of 1.1.2015` `the third part's tables, in the order of 1.1.2015`)

#ASSERT count `the update checks of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 3513
#ASSERT count (`the published misses in` `the update checks of 1.1.2015`) EQUALS 925
#ASSERT `the published worst miss in` `the update checks of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the cells of 1.1.2015 the third part does not print` EQUALS 9

-- The three cells more than an agora off are the three the third part
-- prints two or three agorot below its own update (its finding
-- F-ofek-hadash-tosefet-2011-third-b): א'3 at seniority 2, grade 4; א'6 at
-- seniority 4, grade 2; א'7 at seniority 33, grade 7. Here each is two
-- agorot above the third part's cell raised, as a cell the third part had
-- printed right would be: the tables of 1.1.2015 do not carry its slip.
GIVEN new IS A `published table`, old IS A `salary table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `published cell check`
DECIDE `the cells of 1.1.2015 more than an agora off the update in` new old IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `agorot over the rule` GREATER THAN 1 OR c's `agorot over the rule` LESS THAN (0 MINUS 1))
           (`the published cells beside` (`the third part's cell raised to 1.1.2015 in` old) `in` new)

`the cells of 1.1.2015 off the update are the third part's three slips` MEANS
        map (GIVEN cs YIELD map (GIVEN c YIELD LIST (c's `checked label`), (c's `checked grade`), (c's `agorot over the rule`)) cs)
            (zipWith `the cells of 1.1.2015 more than an agora off the update in` `the seven tables of 1.1.2015` `the third part's tables, in the order of 1.1.2015`)
    EQUALS LIST EMPTY, EMPTY, (LIST (LIST 2, 4, 2)), EMPTY, EMPTY, (LIST (LIST 4, 2, 2)), (LIST (LIST 33, 7, 2))
#ASSERT `the cells of 1.1.2015 off the update are the third part's three slips`
#ASSERT `the cell of` `third-part annex א'3` 2 4 EQUALS JUST 7315.06
#ASSERT `the published cell at` `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015` 2 4 EQUALS JUST 7356.58

-- The nine cells the third part's tables give no value for: cells the
-- corpus reads there as [לא קריא] — the first cell of each table's first
-- row, and one more in א'4 (seniority 29, grade 2.5) and in א'6 (seniority
-- 35, grade 4). Every other cell is checked.
#ASSERT zipWith (GIVEN new, old YIELD `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the third part's cell raised to 1.1.2015 in` old) `in` new) `the seven tables of 1.1.2015` `the third part's tables, in the order of 1.1.2015` EQUALS LIST 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1

-- (3) §46(א): the conversion tables are the salary tables with intermediate
-- grades — every cell א'1 prints, א'3 prints at the same seniority and grade,
-- and א'2's, א'4.
#ASSERT null (`the published misses in` (`the published cells beside` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'1 of 1.1.2015`))
#ASSERT null (`the published misses in` (`the published cells beside` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'4 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015`))
#ASSERT `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'1 of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the same published cell of` `annex א'4 of 1.1.2015`) `in` `annex א'2 of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 0

-- (4) The steps each table prints: 2% a year to the seventh year and 1%
-- from the eighth beside the rows; 7.5% to grades 2–6 and 8.5% to grades
-- 7–9 in the header; and each intermediate grade the mean of its
-- neighbours. Each printed cell beside the cell its step makes of its
-- neighbour, to the agora.
`the step checks of 1.1.2015` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD concat (LIST (`the published cells beside` (`the published row rate of` t) `in` t),
                                             (`the published cells beside` (`the published grade rate of` t) `in` t),
                                             (`the published cells beside` (`the published midway of` t) `in` t)))
                `the seven tables of 1.1.2015`)

#ASSERT count `the step checks of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 6689
#ASSERT count (`the published misses in` `the step checks of 1.1.2015`) EQUALS 1734
#ASSERT `the published worst miss in` `the step checks of 1.1.2015` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `published rate`) (t's `published grade rates`) EQUALS LIST (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (7.5%), (8.5%), (8.5%), (8.5%)) `the seven tables of 1.1.2015`

-- (5) Every table rises along its grades and down its rows, so "the grade
-- nearest at or above A" (§46(ב)) is one cell.
#ASSERT all `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `the seven tables of 1.1.2015`

-- The tables at work: §46's placement on a conversion row.
#ASSERT `the placement in the row` 6000 (`the published row at` `annex א'3 of 1.1.2015` 1) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 1.5 6023.36)
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2015) `annex א'1 of 1.1.2015` 36 9 EQUALS JUST 15999.37
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2014) `annex א'1 of 1.1.2015` 36 9 EQUALS NOTHING
